.TH UPDATE-COW-SPACE 1 "2026-01-09" "arch-remaster" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
update-cow-space \- Update CoW space parameter in GRUB config for Arch live USB

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B update-cow-space
.RI <cow_size>
.RB [ -h | --help ]
.RB [ -v | --version ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
update-cow-space updates the CoW (Copy-on-Write) space parameter in the GRUB configuration for a running Arch Linux live USB. It detects whether the system is running from live USB or in copytoram mode and automatically handles mounting the boot partition if necessary.

The script takes the desired CoW space size as an argument and modifies the GRUB config to add or update the cow_spacesize kernel parameter.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.BR <cow_size>
The CoW space size to set (e.g., 1G, 512M).

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR -h , --help
Display help message and exit.

.TP
.BR -v , --version
Display version information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES

Update CoW space to 1G on a running live USB:
.RS
.PP
.nf
sudo update-cow-space 1G
.fi
.RE

.SH NOTES
This script requires root privileges and should be run on an Arch Linux live USB environment. It will detect copytoram mode and mount the EFI partition if needed. Reboot the USB after updating to apply changes.

.SH AUTHOR
Written by Adrian <adrian@mxlinux.org> for the arch-remaster project.

